# maternalcontinuum
An R package for calculating the Maternal Healthcare Continuum (CoC) from cross-sectional survey data. 
This package recodes standard maternal health variables (Antenatal Care, Skilled Birth Attendance, and Postnatal Care) into binary indicators and calculates a woman's overall completion of the continuum of care.
## Installation
You can install the development version from GitHub:
```r
# install.packages("devtools")
devtools::install_github("Ch-127/maternalcontinuum")

  Usage
library(maternalcontinuum)
library(haven)

# Load your survey data (e.g., SPSS)
df <- read_sav("your_survey_data.sav")

# Calculate the continuum of care
df_clean <- calculate_continuum(
  data = df, 
  anc_var = "Antenatalcarevisit", 
  sba_var = "deliverywithskilledbirthattendant", 
  pnc_var = "postnatalcare"
)

# View completion rates
table(df_clean$CoC_completion)

